   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 533 of the laws of 2011 relating to creating the Norwood public library in the towns of Potsdam and Stockholm, county of St. Lawrence, in relation to the requirements on a petition for a person to be placed on the ballot for election of a trustee",
    "basePrintNo": "S7588",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7588-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 533 of 2011",
    "lawSection": "Public Libraries",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7588\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend chapter 533 of the laws of 2011 relating to creating\nthe Norwood public library in the towns of Potsdam and Stockholm,\ncounty of St. Lawrence, in relation to the requirements on a petition\nfor a person to be placed on the ballot for election of a trustee\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo change the number of required signatures on a petition for a person\nto be placed on the ballot for election of a trustee from 50 to 25\nsignatures.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one amends subdivision 3 of section 2 of Chapter 533 of the\nlaws 2011, relating to creating the Norwood public library, changing\nthe number of required signatures on a petition for a person to be\nplaced on the ballot for election of a trustee from 50 to 25 voters.\n\nSection two provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis legislation has been requested by the Norwood Public Library\nBoard. The library is extremely small and is located in a sparsely\npopulated, rural district - making obtaining 50 signatures very\ndifficult. Larger, nearby libraries require only 25 signatures.  This\nlegislation will adjust the required signatures to 25, which is more\nrealistic for interested parties.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediate.\n",
